:: Restore the classic (Windows 10) right-click context menu in Windows 11.
:: Creates a registry key under HKCU that forces Explorer to use the old-style context menu.
:: Usage: Run this in an elevated Command Prompt (Run as administrator).
:: After running: restart Explorer or sign out/sign in for changes to take effect.
:: Notes:
:: - This only modifies the current user's registry (HKCU).
:: - /f forces overwriting without prompt; /ve sets the default (empty) value.
:: - Back up your registry or create a System Restore point before making changes.

reg.exe add "HKCU\Software\Classes\CLSID\{86ca1aa0-34aa-4e8b-a509-50c905bae2a2}\InprocServer32" /f /ve
